rm had no prior coverage. Neutering the direct-basis exemption at fold.go:1629 instead fails TestMergeSuccessorRestingOnThePredecessorItRetiresStaysCurrent and TestMergePlanIsNotLentToARecordTheMergeDidNotPublish by name while the new test passes, so no coverage was stolen in either direction. Both mutations reverted before commit.\n\nGates actually run at this exact head: gofmt -l ./internal empty, git diff --check clean, go vet ./... exit 0, go test ./... -count=1 exit 0 with all 30 packages ok and no FAIL or panic.","body":{"commit":"dafae40f4371d23a18e286e6c2773753b3d9ee76","path":"internal/workroom"}}